id: pmc-audience-contracts
title: Publish audience-specific change contracts with shared attribution
description: "Project explicitly tagged API-user, operator and agent-behavior facets of delivered items into versioned change contracts. Reuse release selection, section rules and resolution prose; core item metadata owns facet declarations."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T16:46:26.490Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:43:57.881Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:43:57.865Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T21:43:57.865Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Each audience sees only declared facets; missing facets yield omissions rather than invented prose; byte-stable fixtures cover mixed releases; typed SDK and CLI provide compact TOON/JSON and typed refusals with remedies; docs and read-only public tracker validation without git; npm and Bun CI release gates pass.
resolution: "Declared audience facets produce isolated notes and explicit omissions with a shared deterministic attribution ledger, compact no-git SDK/CLI and full npm/Bun CI evidence."
expected_result: Each audience sees only declared facets; missing facets yield omissions rather than invented prose; byte-stable fixtures cover mixed releases; typed SDK and CLI provide compact TOON/JSON and typed refusals with remedies; docs and read-only public tracker validation without git; npm and Bun CI release gates pass.
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/271, merged 2026-10-23T18:06:54Z, merge 80e387dc23769b22a0729158c08b7e45f3c19395: Declared audience facets produce isolated notes and explicit omissions with a shared deterministic attribution ledger, compact no-git SDK/CLI and full npm/Bun CI evidence."
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T16:46:46.585Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: core SDK provides extensible ItemMetadata, structured JSON mutation, certified listAllComplete reads and expected-error contracts; no audience-facet release publisher found. pm-brief summarizes current context and acknowledged handoffs, not versioned releases. Reuse buildChangelogDocument selection, grouping, section rules and close_reason rendering. Store explicit change_facets in core item metadata; no core or sibling changes. Public validation uses a read-only non-git tracker copy."
  "2026-10-23T16:50:47.707Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed audience contracts, shared prose-free attribution ledger and SHA-256 identity, compact TOON/JSON, and expected-error refusals with remedies. Registered change_facets through the core field API and use certified listAllComplete reads; no parallel metadata store. Missing declarations and unavailable explicitly requested close_reason prose emit omissions. Added mixed-release golden fixtures and no-git SDK, standalone and real host coverage."
  "2026-10-23T16:53:43.674Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public main snapshot validation: 193 certified items, 183 closed, 179 selected changes after four non-change dispositions, 36 release groups, zero pre-existing facet declarations. Correctly published zero notes and 537 explicit omissions. JSON 35176 bytes; TOON 19219 bytes; warm SDK projection 611 ms. All 396 tracker files and membership unchanged; SDK and standalone bytes matched and TOON round-tripped. Each audience retained the same ledger SHA-256. See docs/audience-contract-validation.md. Positive fixtures separately cover three changes, four notes and five omissions across mixed releases."
  "2026-10-23T16:55:04.145Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: changing only buildAudienceContracts back to unscoped title publication made the mixed-release regression fail (exit 1). Restoring title fallback for missing close_reason made the explicit-facet regression fail (exit 1). Restored production behavior after each probe. Targeted module coverage currently measures 100% lines/functions; added both ID-ordering comparator arms for the unchanged 100% branch gate. No standalone lint script is configured; use the repository docstring gate and diff whitespace check alongside typecheck."
  "2026-10-23T17:00:27.924Z",codex-agent,"Targeted local regression command passed 199/199 tests, zero failures/skips. Production and test typechecks passed. Docstring lint passed for 22 files and 192 declarations; diff whitespace check passed. Core structured field mutation and real extension/standalone no-git flows are covered. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI at unchanged thresholds to avoid loading the shared host. Existing pm CLI strict create policy required the documented progressive create mode; no core bug found."
  "2026-10-23T17:01:35.415Z",codex-agent,"Final actual-host mutation check caught a package manifest activation gap: command-only lazy activation prevented change_facets registration during core update. Removed that restriction so schema fields activate for core mutations, as in schema-owning sibling packages. Added a real no-git pm update --field regression; rerunning the five contract tests and module coverage. This is a package integration correction, not a core defect. Linked-test execution receipts are disabled by existing project policy; outcomes are recorded here without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-23T17:02:30.881Z",codex-agent,"Final contract coverage passed 5/5 tests with zero failures/skips and 100% measured lines, branches and functions for both new modules, through pm test --run --progress --only-last. Actual core CLI field mutation now passes without git. Local targeted suite passed 199/199; production/test typecheck, 192-declaration docstring lint and whitespace checks passed. Behavioral revert probes both failed as expected. Implementation is ready for PR and unchanged-threshold npm/Bun CI verification. Remaining validation boundaries: public corpus has no native facets; positive facets use synthetic fixtures; hosted transports were not exercised. No unresolved implementation blocker; no core bug found."
  "2026-10-23T17:12:12.119Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/271 is ready for review. Implementation head 28a22165818689c6349911a8a8fb6ab9bf18f806 passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39992106138: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 827/827 tests, zero failures/skips, on Node 22 and 26 (four gate executions). All 19 measured source files met 100% lines/branches/functions; direct Bun CLI/SDK smoke passed 2/2 on each node job. CodeQL and Semgrep passed. External automated review remains missing evidence: services skipped or lacked review capacity. This receipt changes tracker evidence only; final-head CI will be verified before handoff. Claim remains released and item stays in progress for orchestrator closure."
  "2026-10-23T17:26:56.833Z",codex-agent,"Review blocked PR 271 on unsupported JSON form-feed/backspace escapes in the audience TOON formatter. Remote branch is current and main has not advanced; reuse this item. Replace hand-built TOON with the exact encoder version used by the pinned core CLI and decode regressions through the core SDK testing decoder. Cover form feed, backspace, NUL, unit separator, quotes, backslashes and newlines; prove failure with only the formatter reverted. Keep dependency pins for core unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T17:30:24.411Z",codex-agent,"Fixed the blocking TOON review finding by replacing manual JSON-based quoting with the TOON 4.4.0 report encoder, the exact library version used by the pinned pm CLI; core pins are unchanged. Tests now use decodeToon from the pm SDK. New regression: control-character facets round-trip through the pm TOON decoder. It covers form feed, backspace, NUL, unit separator, quotes, backslashes, newlines, carriage returns and tabs. Reverting only formatAudienceContracts fails that test with Invalid escape sequence: form feed (exit 1); restored encoder passes. All six contract tests passed with 100% measured lines/branches/functions for both modules; typecheck, test typecheck, 192-declaration docstring lint and whitespace checks passed. Core decoder accepts valid Unicode control escapes, so no upstream decoder repro is needed. Reused read-only public snapshot: TOON is now 18091 bytes; JSON, attribution fingerprint and all 396 source files unchanged. Updated the TOON golden fixture and docs."
  "2026-10-23T17:43:38.764Z",codex-agent,"Re-review blocked PR 271 on input-dependent section ordering for type-grouped contracts with an undated item. Reuse this item and retain finished validation. Reproduce the exact two dated Tasks plus undated Feature in every permutation, then canonicalize contract section and item ordering before assigning attribution indices and hashing the ledger. Preserve generator-owned membership, classification and prose rules; verify formatter fixes remain intact."
  "2026-10-23T17:48:07.192Z",codex-agent,The same synthetic three-item case also exposes a pre-existing non-transitive ordinary generator comparator. Deduplicated and recorded out-of-scope follow-up pmc-total-item-order; this PR fixes contract canonicalization without changing ordinary changelog presentation.
  "2026-10-23T17:51:31.249Z",codex-agent,"Fixed contract determinism using total UTF-16 keys: normalize input rows by unique item ID before generator selection, then order each release by section heading and item ID before assigning attribution indices or hashing. No optional date/title comparator influences contract identity; generator membership, section classification and prose remain reused. Regression reviewer items preserve contract bytes and attribution in all permutations covers all six permutations of Task A dated October 19, undated Feature B and Task C dated October 20 across four section modes, three release modes and each audience. Reverting only buildAudienceContracts fails with ledger section/index differences (exit 1); restored implementation passes. Seven contract tests passed, with 100% measured lines/branches/functions in both modules. Production/test typechecks and docstring lint passed. Reversed public snapshot now matches JSON and TOON bytes exactly: 179 changes, 36 releases, 537 omissions; JSON 35176 bytes, TOON 18091 bytes; all 396 source files unchanged. Canonical ledger SHA-256 is eb76c5124ccf69d3338224b045f8bb07724f7dd48f49a47919c92c05c5626bb9. Broader ordinary-generator sorting is tracked in pmc-total-item-order."
